title The writer that knew one shape
prompt the tail of this lap -- the send's own guard reddened after the claim close landed
rota none -- the rota was read and recorded at 20260917.010537; this is that lap's own send repair
think The claim-close commit ran tools/r/remember_git_nib.rish write before committing, which is what rule 5 of .claude/rules/remember-git-nib.md asks of a follow-up. The guard reddened afterwards.
think The tool derives git rev-parse HEAD^ and writes that. For rule 2, the amend after the final rebase, HEAD^ is exactly right. For rule 5, the follow-up landing on top of the work commit, the card wants HEAD itself, because that HEAD becomes the follow-up's parent.
think So the tool wrote the grandparent, and the card named a hash that is none of the three honest states the witness accepts.
think Proven rather than assumed: I reset hard to the pushed commit and re-read the guard there. Still RED. That is what told a stale pin apart from a local mistake of my own making.
obs My first repair was an amend of a commit already pushed to xy, and xy refused it as a non-fast-forward. The refusal was right and I did not force. The rebase that followed turned my correction into a pin-only commit, which .claude/rules/remember-git-nib.md keeps off the remote by name -- so the fix had to become a commit carrying real content, which is this row and this log.
obs The lesson past my own slip: a law with two shapes and a tool with one is a law half-automated, and the automated half is the one everybody reaches for. The writer exists because a hand falsified the nib four times in ninety minutes; a tool correct on one path and silently one short on the other is worse than that hand, because its answer carries no doubt.
obs Named and not built. This lap already carries a closed row and its own send, and a writer repaired inside a send is how a repair becomes its own red. The row carries the workaround for whoever meets it first: hand the hash to remember_git_nib_write.sh yourself.
file construction/REDS.md REDS %803 booked, OPEN, with the repair specified and the workaround named
file construction/ITINERARY.md the Git nib pinned to this commit's parent by hand, which is rule 5's own shape
scope one row booked, no tool changed
status GREEN -- remember_git_nib, reds_pin_capacity, reds_ledger_monotone and reds_status_consistency GREEN on the staged tree
recommend keep-going -- %803 is a small bounded repair: one mode argument on remember_git_nib.rish and a refusal to guess, with its pen proving both shapes
